meta {
  name: identity
}

auth {
  mode: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{identityApiKey}}
}

docs {
  Management API of a portitor-identity (docs/api/identity-management-openapi.json):
  the provider's in the "single" environment, the consumer's in "two-connectors"
  (identityMgmtUrl; its DID is identityDid). Put that identity's key
  (target/vscode-dcp/<provider or consumer>/identity-management.key) in the
  environment's secret identityApiKey.
  "DID document" and "Health (public port)" call the same identity's public port
  (identityUrl, docs/api/identity-openapi.json) and need no key. Its STS is in
  "auth/STS token". The credential service (presentations/query, credentials, offers)
  takes tokens of other participants, so it has no request here: the provider and the
  issuer call it.
}
